  "title": "test: Convert to the same path separators on MSYS2",
  "description": "On the MSYS2 fork of CPython, os.sep and os.altsep are swapped when\nrunning inside a MSYS2 environment (bash shell, as when compiling\nand testing.) That affects what os.path.join does in unicode_env.\n\nwsutil/filesystem does not consistently use g_build_filename and\ng_path_get_basename, but instead always assumes that G_DIR_SEPARATOR_S\n('\\') will be used on Windows, including MSYS2, which can lead to\nmixed slash paths when the APPDATA environment variable has forward\nslashes. There may also be a bug related to g_build_filename in GLib\nwhen the first element has a drive letter and does not have an explicit\nseparator at the end either.\n\nNormalize the path for now so that MSYS2 will pass the test.",
